  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a fix plan, but haven't changed any code yet because plan mode is on. I couldn't submit the plan for approval the usual way (that tool isn't available here), so please tell me if you want me to go ahead.\n\n**Cause:** Completion splits the command line using Python's `shlex` in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py:603`). By default, `shlex` treats `#` as the start of a comment and throws away everything after it. So `cli --opt a#b` is read as `[\"cli\", \"--opt\", \"a\"]`, and completion works on the wrong input.\n\n**Planned fix** (saved in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-rosy-wave.md`):\n1. In `split_arg_string`, add `lex.commenters = \"\"` right after `lex.whitespace_split = True`, so `#` is read as a normal character.\n2. Add test cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `cli a#b`, `cli #a`, and `cli 'my #file` (with an unclosed quote).\n3. Optionally, add an end-to-end completion test in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`, for example a choice option whose values contain `#`.\n4. Add a `CHANGES.md` entry under a new unreleased 8.5.1 section, since 8.5.0 is already released.\n\n**To check it:** run `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, then the full test suite.",
